# ─── Rust ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored — this is an application, so the lock
# file should be committed for reproducible builds. (Uncomment below only if the
# server is ever published as a library crate.)
# Cargo.lock

# ─── Node / Frontend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
ui/dist-ssr/
ui/*.local

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ─── Tauri ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ui/src-tauri/target/
ui/src-tauri/gen/

# ─── VSCode ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json   # keep — useful for recommending extensions to contributors
!.vscode/settings.json     # keep — project-level editor settings (rulers, format on save, etc.)
!.vscode/launch.json       # keep — debug launch configs

# ─── macOS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
# macOS custom-folder-icon file (literally "Icon" + a carriage return).
# NOTE: do NOT use `Icon?` here — `?` matches any char and, case-insensitively,
# matches the `icons/` directory, which silently excludes the Tauri app icons.
Icon[\r]
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ─── Linux ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*~
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*

# ─── Windows ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ─── Environment / Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ─── mise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# mise installs tools globally; nothing project-local to ignore

# ─── git-atlas runtime files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The server writes a port lockfile at runtime — not for version control
# (stored in platform data dir, not repo root — nothing to ignore here)
